    "body": "<!-- crb-followup-result:v1 harvest=728 -->\n### Triage result\n\nEpic: #732\n\n- #733 [followups-728 01/07] Cover the untested branches in the boundary, filter-compiler and relation-cardinality tests\n- #734 [followups-728 02/07] Remove dead test code, share the manifestPath helper, and end the scratch-schema pool on setup failure\n- #735 [followups-728 03/07] Share the Inbox tick test helpers and reuse the validated target database in confirm\n- #736 [followups-728 04/07] Keep the original error on the mail ingest conflict and discovery rollback paths\n- #737 [followups-728 05/07] Serialize worker reconciliation passes and correct the drift check's snapshot comment\n- #738 [followups-728 06/07] Reject out-of-range PORT values and non-ISO AI usage report dates at their edges\n- #739 [followups-728 07/07] Drop the unused runtime pg dependency from @semprec/ai-gateway\n\n#### Rejected (13)\n\n| PR | Key | Verdict | Reason | Tracked by |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #284 | d56c2ea8b0 | already-fixed | backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/inboxTickProposal.test.ts:53: Commit 0af2f59 ('Scan every sourceInbox edge in the proposal test helper and cover the rejected lock'): findProposalForItem now iterates every edge and skips soft-deleted proposals (lines 53-60) instead of taking edges[0]. |  |\n| #284 | e37b961cd0 | already-fixed | backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/inboxTickProposal.test.ts:237: Commit 0af2f59: the lock test is now it.each([\"confirmed\", \"rejected\"]), so the rejected branch of LOCKED_PROPOSAL_STATUSES is exercised. |  |\n| #286 | 3ddbf0f6ac | already-fixed | backend/packages/data/src/inbox/inboxTickAction.ts:213: The unknown-entityKind guard is no longer unreachable: confirm now reads the envelope from the stored JSONB column via a cast (proposalActions.ts:249) and passes it to assertValidProposalEnvelope (proposalActions.ts:137), so the guard at inboxTickAction.ts:213-221 validates a value that did not come from computeProposalEnvelope. |  |\n| #293 | 927787b2ff | already-fixed | backend/packages/module-registry/src/registry.ts:478: Commit 16a24cb ([module-contract 02/12], merged after PR #293's last-seen head) reads loaded.exports in the projection methods (registry.ts:478, 479, 501, 502, 544, 561). |  |\n| #300 | 9c430a7339 | invalid | backend/packages/data/src/moduleWorkers.ts:76: The bot's scenario (two different workers with the same workerName) cannot occur: ModuleRegistry rejects a worker name already claimed by any module (registry.ts:368-395, workerNameOwners, present since c83576a, before PR #300). workerInstanceId is `${workerName}@${rowId}`, so a duplicate id inside the per-row loop comes from the named worker itself (a repeated row id), which is what the message says. |  |\n| #308 | 33a71227e9 | already-fixed | backend/packages/data/src/notifications/findings.ts:12: Commit 3c71ed7 rewrote the comment: it now cites migration 0030, and 0030_notifications_schema.sql:27-29 creates the partial unique index manifest_drift_findings_active_idx. |  |\n| #309 | b3e1bad7b6 | not-worth | backend/packages/module-boundaries/src/__tests__/module-boundaries.unit.test.ts:46: The service-to-module boundary is being deleted: open issue #653 removes the modules/ boundary rules (including no-service-to-module) from backend/dependency-cruiser.rules.json and deletes fixtures/modules/** and svcB/src/badModuleImport.ts. A test for a service importing a module's public entry would test a rule scheduled for removal. (Since issue #173 that import is also forbidden, not allowed as the finding assumed.) |  |\n| #313 | 06f2666876 | already-fixed | backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/libraryMailInboxModuleManifests.unit.test.ts:61: The file was renamed to *.unit.test.ts in da00707; commit 26ede5f ('Assert the mail sync manifest's heartbeat actions exactly') replaced expect.arrayContaining with an exact toEqual at line 61. |  |\n| #314 | 7b313f676d | already-fixed | backend/packages/data/src/seed/seedTenDatabases.ts:474: Commit ad71179 ('Add stable database keys and nullable system names (#235)') removed the filter/map chain and its `as string` cast; the code now reads manifestDatabase?.defaultViewType ?? \"table\". |  |\n| #318 | 12e99d1122 | invalid | backend/packages/data/src/seed/seedEmailModule.ts:231: The finding compares the code with PR #318's description, not with a requirement. cardinality: \"one_to_many\" is correct: ingestAttachments creates a fresh File item per attachment and links it (mail/attachments.ts:134-139), so a File never belongs to two Emails. Only the PR description was stale; nothing in the repository is wrong. |  |\n| #322 | 08fbcfd87b | already-fixed | backend/packages/agent-runtime/src/lifecycleAdapter.ts: pushLiveEvent no longer exists anywhere in backend/ (git grep returns nothing); it was removed by commit 9445e7a ('Replay and stream watched agent runs'). |  |\n| #326 | 428990da25 | already-fixed | backend/packages/ai-gateway/src/gateway.ts:26: Commit 2e96ef9 ('Read the AI budgets and the timezone from one settings snapshot') replaced the two reads with one getAiBudgetsWithTimezone(client) call. |  |\n| #328 | 3c3f238235 | already-fixed | backend/packages/data/src/inbox/inboxRouteHandlers.ts:55: Commit 64a125c (#239, merged after PR #328) validates credential.plaintext as a non-empty string at the confirm route (inboxRouteHandlers.ts:55-56), the only caller of confirmProposalWithClient (inboxRouteHandlers.ts:74); an empty plaintext is rejected with a ValidationError before it reaches storeCredential. |  |\n\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=284 key=d56c2ea8b0 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=284 key=e37b961cd0 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=286 key=3ddbf0f6ac -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=293 key=927787b2ff -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=300 key=9c430a7339 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=308 key=33a71227e9 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=309 key=b3e1bad7b6 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=313 key=06f2666876 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=314 key=7b313f676d -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=318 key=12e99d1122 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=322 key=08fbcfd87b -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=326 key=428990da25 -->\n<!-- crb-followup:v1 pr=328 key=3c3f238235 -->\n\n#### Advisories\n\nNone.\n",
